<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.dailybriefing</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py</string>
        <string>--daily-briefing</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Runs twice a day, 9:00am and 5:00pm, for every customer by
         default (see daily_briefing()'s docstring in curant-cli --
         originally Grace-exclusive at a single 7am slot, opened up to
         everyone and moved to this cadence per the owner's direction).
         StartCalendarInterval accepts an array for multiple fire times
         -- this is one job that runs twice daily, not two separate jobs. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>9</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>0</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>17</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>0</integer>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-dailybriefing.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-dailybriefing-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp com.curant.dailybriefing.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.dailybriefing.plist

On by default for every customer (config["daily_briefing_enabled"]
defaults to True in curant-cli's daily_briefing() -- a customer can turn
it off with `curant-cli set-daily-briefing off`). This should be
installed as part of standard setup going forward, same as
com.curant.proactive.plist and com.curant.watcher.plist.

To test immediately rather than waiting for 9am/5pm, run
curant-watcher.py with the --daily-briefing flag directly (see
ProgramArguments above).

Logs land at /tmp/curant-dailybriefing.log and /tmp/curant-dailybriefing-error.log.
-->
